  "prefLabel": "Rev 401.30 Surviving spouse",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 401.30 “Surviving spouse” means a person who was the spouse of a person at the time of the person’s death, and who has not remarried, or who has remarried but was later divorced. The term does not include a person who has remarried and the new spouse dies.\n\nSource. #12027, eff 10-28-16; renumbered by #12925 (formerly Rev 401.29)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev400.html"
